 ## Tests
 
 Jest specs live under `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs`, beside `jest.config.luau`, whose
-`testMatch` picks up every ModuleScript named `*.spec`. Specs run only in Studio, which this
-project can't reach, so check specs with the commands below like any other file.
+`testMatch` picks up every ModuleScript named `*.spec`. Locally, specs run only in Studio, which
+this project can't reach, so check specs with the commands below like any other file.
+
+### CI
+
+`.github/workflows/specs.yml` runs the specs on every pull request: it installs packages,
+builds `default.project.json` with Rojo, publishes the build as a new version of a dedicated CI
+place, and runs `ci/run-specs.luau` against that version through Open Cloud's Luau Execution API.
+The pull request fails if any spec fails, any spec file fails to load, or no specs are found.
+Jest's output is in the job's "Task logs" group, and failures are summarized on the run page.
+
+It needs three repository secrets: `ROBLOX_UNIVERSE_ID` and `ROBLOX_PLACE_ID` (the CI place,
+which every run overwrites) and `ROBLOX_API_KEY` (an Open Cloud key with
+`universe-places:write` and `universe.place.luau-execution-session:read`/`:write` on that
+universe). Pull requests from forks don't get the secrets, so their runs fail.
+
+In CI, Jest can't use `debug.loadmodule`, so modules are cached across spec files rather than
+loaded fresh for each one. Don't rely on module state being reset between spec files.
 
 ## Checks
 
